<item><title>Tunisia says alternative sentences exclude crimes</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/tunisia-says-alternative-sentences-exclude-crimes-e45200/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/tunisia-says-alternative-sentences-exclude-crimes-e45200/</guid><category>Tunisia</category><description>Justice Minister Leïla Jaffel told Parliament the measures apply only to eligible offences and require the convicted person’s consent.</description><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 06:12:24 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/tunisia-says-alternative-sentences-exclude-crimes-e45200/share.jpg" length="39401" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/tunisia-says-alternative-sentences-exclude-crimes-e45200/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
